    "answer": {
      "short": "Bottles are the best buy: £0.63/L compared with £0.76/L for cans. Equivalently, bottles give 1.6 L per £1 and cans give 1.32 L per £1.",
      "worked": "Bottles:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Volume}&=2\\times2=4\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Price per litre}&=\\frac{£2.50}{4}=£0.625\\approx £0.63\\end{align*}$$\nCans:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Volume}&=16\\times330=5280\\text{ mL}=5.28\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Price per litre}&=\\frac{£4}{5.28}=£\\frac{25}{33}\\approx £0.76\\end{align*}$$\nBottles are the best buy because their price per litre is lower.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
